e-ramses_esp","content":"2\\. Setting up the ramses_esp","locale":"en"},"375":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-7","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#opening-the-serial-console","content":"Opening the serial console","locale":"en"},"376":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-8","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"PuTTY settings","locale":"en"},"377":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-9","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"Setting up Wi-Fi and MQTT","locale":"en"},"378":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-10","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"Elecram ESP32-C6 board","locale":"en"},"379":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-11","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#topics","content":"Topics","locale":"en"},"380":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-12","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#3-installing-the-app","content":"3\\. Installing the app","locale":"en"},"381":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-13","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#4-adding-devices","content":"4\\. Adding devices","locale":"en"},"382":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-14","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"Part","locale":"en"},"383":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-15","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"384":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-16","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"**Homey Pro (2023)** or **Homey Pro mini**","locale":"en"},"385":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-17","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"Firmware **12.4 or newer**. The app runs locally; Homey Cloud is not supported.","locale":"en"},"386":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-18","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"**ramses_esp**","locale":"en"},"387":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-19","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"An ESP32 with an 868 MHz radio and the ramses_esp firmware, connected to your Wi-Fi. See which gateway for boards you can buy.","locale":"en"},"388":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-20","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"**MQTT broker**","locale":"en"},"389":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-21","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"Where the ramses_esp publishes to. The easiest is the *MQTT Broker* app on Homey itself; Mosquitto on a NAS or Raspberry Pi works just as well.","locale":"en"},"390":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-22","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"**A RAMSES II ventilation system**","locale":"en"},"391":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-23","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"Orcon, Itho, Vasco, ClimaRad or Nuaire on 868 MHz.","locale":"en"},"392":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-24","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#what-you-need","content":"Place the ramses_esp somewhere between your Homey Wi-Fi and the ventilation unit. 868 MHz passes walls well, but an\nattic with a concrete floor in between can be just too much. The bus view shows the signal\nstrength (RSSI) of every packet.","locale":"en"},"393":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-25","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"These boards are tested with the app. Both come with the right firmware, so you only set up Wi-Fi and MQTT\n(step 2 below).","locale":"en"},"394":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-26","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"Board","locale":"en"},"395":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-27","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"Chip","locale":"en"},"396":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-28","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"Firmware","locale":"en"},"397":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-29","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"Where","locale":"en"},"398":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-30","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"**Elecram Sub-GHz 855–925 MHz Bridge**","locale":"en"},"399":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-31","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"ESP32-C6 + TI CC1101","locale":"en"},"400":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-32","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"ramses_esp for ESP32-C6 (reports as `ramses_esp_c6`)","locale":"en"},"401":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-33","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"elecram.com. Order the 868 MHz antenna with it.","locale":"en"},"402":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-34","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"**Indalo-Tech RAMSES_ESP**","locale":"en"},"403":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-35","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"ESP32-S3 + TI CC1101","locale":"en"},"404":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-36","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"ramses_esp (reports as `ramses_esp`)","locale":"en"},"405":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-37","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"indalotech.co.uk, when the shop is open.","locale":"en"},"406":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-38","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#which-gateway","content":"The app reads both firmwares the same way: it finds gateways by their MQTT topics, not by firmware name. Setting up\nthe Elecram board has a few extra points; see Elecram ESP32-C6 board.","locale":"en"},"407":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-39","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#1-the-mqtt-broker","content":"The ramses_esp and Homey don't talk to each other directly, but through an MQTT broker.","locale":"en"},"408":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-40","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#option-a-the-mqtt-broker-app-on-homey-recommended","content":"Install the **MQTT Broker** app from the Homey App Store.","locale":"en"},"409":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-41","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#option-a-the-mqtt-broker-app-on-homey-recommended","content":"Open *Apps → MQTT Broker → Configure* and check that the broker listens on port **1883**.","locale":"en"},"410":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-42","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#option-a-the-mqtt-broker-app-on-homey-recommended","content":"Create a user (recommended) and note the user name and password.","locale":"en"},"411":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-43","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#option-a-the-mqtt-broker-app-on-homey-recommended","content":"Note the **IP address of your Homey** (*Settings → General → About*). That will be the broker address.","locale":"en"},"412":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-44","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#option-a-the-mqtt-broker-app-on-homey-recommended","content":"Give your Homey a fixed IP address in your router (DHCP reservation). If the address changes, the ramses_esp loses\nits connection to the broker.","locale":"en"},"413":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-45","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#option-b-an-existing-broker","content":"Already running Mosquitto (for example from an old Home Assistant setup)? You can simply keep it. Just make sure\nHomey can reach the broker and that you have the user name and password. TLS (`mqtts`) is supported.","locale":"en"},"414":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-46","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#2-setting-up-the-ramses_esp","content":"Homey cannot talk to the stick over USB serial, so the ramses_esp has to connect to the MQTT broker over **Wi-Fi**.\nYou set this up **once** through the serial console. After that the stick only needs power: a USB charger or a free\nUSB port will do.","locale":"en"},"415":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-47","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#2-setting-up-the-ramses_esp","content":"**Coming from Home Assistant?** There the stick usually hung off the Raspberry Pi over USB serial. Unplug it and\nconfigure it as below. You won't need your ramses_cc configuration any more, but keep the *FAN ID* and the remote\naddress: you'll need them in Homey.","locale":"en"},"416":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-48","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#opening-the-serial-console","content":"Plug the ramses_esp into a Windows, macOS or Linux computer.","locale":"en"},"417":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-49","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#opening-the-serial-console","content":"Open a serial terminal on the right port at **115200 baud**:","locale":"en"},"418":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-50","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#opening-the-serial-console","content":"**Windows**: PuTTY, connection type *Serial*. Find the COM port in\n*Device Manager → Ports (COM & LPT)*. Set PuTTY up as below before you click *Open*.","locale":"en"},"419":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-51","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#opening-the-serial-console","content":"**macOS / Linux**: for example `screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200` (on macOS something like `/dev/tty.usbserial-…`).","locale":"en"},"420":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-52","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#opening-the-serial-console","content":"Press **Enter**. You get the ramses_esp prompt.","locale":"en"},"421":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-53","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Where in PuTTY","locale":"en"},"422":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-54","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"423":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-55","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Why","locale":"en"},"424":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-56","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"*Session*","locale":"en"},"425":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-57","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Connection type **Serial**, serial line **COM…**, speed **115200**","locale":"en"},"426":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-58","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"The port of the board.","locale":"en"},"427":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-59","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"*Connection → Serial*","locale":"en"},"428":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-60","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Flow control **None**","locale":"en"},"429":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-61","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"With the default *XON/XOFF* the board receives nothing you type.","locale":"en"},"430":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-62","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"*Terminal*","locale":"en"},"431":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-63","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"**Implicit CR in every LF** on","locale":"en"},"432":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-64","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Lines start at the left instead of running down like stairs.","locale":"en"},"433":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-65","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"*Terminal*","locale":"en"},"434":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-66","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Local echo **Force on**, local line editing **Force on**","locale":"en"},"435":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-67","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"You see what you type and can correct it before *Enter*.","locale":"en"},"436":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-68","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#putty-settings","content":"Save these under a name on the *Session* page, so you can open them with a double click next time. Close PuTTY before\nyou flash the board: only one program can use the COM port at a time.","locale":"en"},"437":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-69","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"Type the commands one by one. They are **case sensitive**.","locale":"en"},"438":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-70","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"Command","locale":"en"},"439":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-71","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"440":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-72","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"`wifi password` / `wifi ssid`","locale":"en"},"441":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-73","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"The password and name of your Wi-Fi network. Use a **2.4 GHz** network; an ESP32 does not support 5 GHz.","locale":"en"},"442":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-74","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"`wifi restart`","locale":"en"},"443":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-75","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"Reconnects with the new Wi-Fi details.","locale":"en"},"444":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-76","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"`mqtt user` / `mqtt password`","locale":"en"},"445":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-77","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"The user you created in the broker app. Leave out if your broker needs no login.","locale":"en"},"446":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-78","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"`mqtt broker`","locale":"en"},"447":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-79","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"The address of the broker. With the MQTT Broker app that is `mqtt://<IP of your Homey>:1883`.","locale":"en"},"448":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-80","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"`sntp server` / `timezone`","locale":"en"},"449":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-81","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"Time synchronisation, so the timestamps in the messages are right. Use your own time zone.","locale":"en"},"450":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-82","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"`reset`","locale":"en"},"451":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-83","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"Restarts the ramses_esp with the new settings.","locale":"en"},"452":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-84","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"**Always set the password before the ssid or broker line.** As soon as the ramses_esp gets an ssid or a broker, it\ntries to connect right away. If the password isn't there yet, that first attempt fails.","locale":"en"},"453":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-85","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"After the `reset` the stick connects to your Wi-Fi and the broker. You can then unplug it from the computer and power\nit somewhere else, ideally halfway between your Homey Wi-Fi and the ventilation unit.","locale":"en"},"454":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-86","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#setting-up-wi-fi-and-mqtt","content":"More commands and firmware updates are in the ramses_esp documentation.","locale":"en"},"455":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-87","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"The Elecram board takes the same commands, with these differences:","locale":"en"},"456":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-88","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"Point","locale":"en"},"457":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-89","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"What to do","locale":"en"},"458":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-90","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"**Network mode**","locale":"en"},"459":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-91","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"The firmware can run over Wi-Fi or Zigbee; MQTT only works in Wi-Fi mode. Type `network show`. If it says `zigbee`, type `network wifi`; the board saves it and restarts.","locale":"en"},"460":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-92","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"**Broker address**","locale":"en"},"461":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-93","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"Type it in full, with `mqtt://` and the port: `mqtt broker mqtt://192.168.1.20:1883`.","locale":"en"},"462":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-94","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"**Changing the MQTT login**","locale":"en"},"463":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-95","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"Type `reset` after `mqtt user` and `mqtt password`. Until then the board keeps retrying with the old login and the console shows `MQTT: Disonnected` over and over.","locale":"en"},"464":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-96","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"**Time**","locale":"en"},"465":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-97","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"The firmware has no time server by default, so the timestamps say `1970-01-01`. Set one with `sntp server pool.ntp.org` and a time zone, for example `timezone CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3` (Amsterdam with daylight saving), then `reset`. Homey does not use the timestamps, so this is optional.","locale":"en"},"466":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-98","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"When it works, the console shows:","locale":"en"},"467":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-99","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"In MQTT Explorer the board shows up as `RAMSES/GATEWAY/18:xxxxxx = online` with `info/firmware = ramses_esp_c6`.","locale":"en"},"468":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-100","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#elecram-esp32-c6-board","content":"**Over Zigbee instead of Wi-Fi (experimental, untested).** In Zigbee mode the board can join\nZigbee2MQTT. The fork has a Zigbee2MQTT extension (branch `z2m_support`,\n`z2m/external_extensions/ramses-esp-bridge.mjs`) that passes the packets on to the same `RAMSES/GATEWAY/18:xxxxxx/rx`\nand `/tx` topics, so the app can read them as usual. Zigbee2MQTT must use the same broker as Homey. The extension is\nnot in a release yet and also needs the board's device definition in Zigbee2MQTT. Over Zigbee there is no\nonline/offline status topic, so the gateway's online card and offline warning don't work. Use Wi-Fi unless you\nwant to experiment.","locale":"en"},"469":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-101","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#topics","content":"If all is well, the ramses_esp then publishes on these topics:","locale":"en"},"470":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-102","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#topics","content":"Topic","locale":"en"},"471":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-103","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#topics","content":"Direction","locale":"en"},"472":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-104","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#topics","content":"Content","locale":"e