m board has a few extra points; see Elecram ESP32-C6 board."],[352,"The app speaks RAMSES II, the protocol these brands share. Brands do number their modes differently; the app\ndetects this by itself, or you choose the brand in the settings."],[740,"The brand and model of your unit (also shown under *Settings → Bus → Model*)."],[244,"The broker cannot be reached"],[145,"The card *Any button was pressed* gives in *Button* the word `low`, `medium`, `high`, `auto`, `away`, `off` or `boost`."],[64,"The code is organised in layers. Everything below `lib/homey` runs under plain `node --test`, without Homey."],[725,"The command arrives, but the unit does something else (e.g. *high* instead of *auto*)? Then the\nbrand is wrong. Choose the brand manually."],[534,"The content, in hex"],[279,"The demand goes in the **first** group of the `31E0` (`00 00 DD 00`), in half percent. An Orcon CO2 15RF raises\nand lowers that group with the CO₂ level; the second group (`01 00 DD 00`) does not drive the unit. Version 1.0.0\nput the demand only in the second group, and the unit did not respond: verified with 100 % in either form on the\nsame unit."],[779,"The device card has a **Fan mode** picker:"],[455,"The Elecram board takes the same commands, with these differences:"],[707,"The fan speed is a number from 0 to 4"],[459,"The firmware can run over Wi-Fi or Zigbee; MQTT only works in Wi-Fi mode. Type `network show`. If it says `zigbee`, type `network wifi`; the board saves it and restarts."],[465,"The firmware has no time server by default, so the timestamps say `1970-01-01`. Set one with `sntp server pool.ntp.org` and a time zone, for example `timezone CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3` (Amsterdam with daylight saving), then `reset`. Homey does not use the timestamps, so this is optional."],[252,"The gateway has cards for advanced use: reacting to any packet on the bus, sending raw frames and knowing whether the\ngateway is online. See Flows → Gateway."],[201,"The gateway is the link between Homey and your ramses_esp. All other devices go through it."],[696,"The gateway keeps becoming unavailable"],[239,"The gateway listens all the time and **remembers every device** it hears, also after a Homey restart. That's why Homey\ncan show a list right away when you add a unit, remote or sensor."],[238,"The last packet received, in readable form."],[318,"The last reported CO₂"],[320,"The last reported humidity"],[336,"The link to your ramses_esp. Sees every packet on the bus and remembers every device it hears."],[28,"The message codes the device sends"],[700,"The mode in Homey doesn't match the unit"],[795,"The mode is also updated when someone uses the **physical remote**; Homey hears it on the bus. On the dashboard tile\nthe mode is shown as a word (*Status*)."],[230,"The new device is called *Ramses Gateway*. Feel free to rename it."],[162,"The packet triggers have these tokens:"],[441,"The password and name of your Wi-Fi network. Use a **2.4 GHz** network; an ESP32 does not support 5 GHz."],[426,"The port of the board."],[234,"The RAMSES address of the ramses_esp, e.g. `18:203612`."],[24,"The RAMSES address, e.g. `29:233244`"],[407,"The ramses_esp and Homey don't talk to each other directly, but through an MQTT broker."],[630,"The ramses_esp hears its own transmissions back. Homey recognises them as an **echo**: they don't count as a remote\nbutton press and they're marked in the bus view. A flow that controls the unit therefore never fires its own trigger."],[260,"The ramses_esp is not connected to this broker. Check its MQTT settings, or enter its address (`18:xxxxxx`) under *Gateway address*."],[248,"The ramses_esp reports offline"],[33,"The role is determined from the messages a device sends. A device reporting `31DA` or `31D9` is a unit, a device\nsending `22F1` is a remote, and so on."],[595,"The same number in `22F1` means something different per brand:"],[282,"The sensor has three action cards:"],[70,"The site lives in `website/` and is built with Fumadocs (Next.js, static export). The\nEnglish pages are in `website/content/docs/en/`, the Dutch ones in `website/content/docs/nl/`, under the **same file\nnames** so the language switcher keeps you on the same page. The order of the sidebar is in each folder's\n`meta.json`; the landing page is `website/app/[lang]/(home)/page.tsx`. View it locally:"],[278,"The unit answered within a second of the first offer. Right after, Homey's reports reach the unit:"],[698,"The unit doesn't respond to Homey"],[324,"The unit has to be in **Auto** to respond to the ventilation demand. Set it to low or high manually and it ignores\nsensors until you set it back."],[789,"The unit regulates itself based on its sensors (CO₂, humidity)"],[196,"The unit still responds to the button as usual; Homey only listens in."],[726,"The unit was not in binding mode. On an Orcon: unplug, plug back in, and start binding **within 2 minutes**. Other\nbrands: see your unit's manual (look for *registering a remote* or *pairing*)."],[445,"The user you created in the broker app. Leave out if your broker needs no login."],[2,"The ventilation on your dashboard, and a look under the hood."],[12,"The widget shows:"],[17,"The widget works in the light and dark theme."],[89,"Then…"],[93,"Then…"],[97,"Then…"],[393,"These boards are tested with the app. Both come with the right firmware, so you only set up Wi-Fi and MQTT\n(step 2 below)."],[151,"These cards are for those who want to go deeper. You'll need some knowledge of the protocol."],[49,"This documentation"],[332,"This Homey app connects to that broker and turns what happens on the bus into regular Homey devices:"],[366,"This is an **unofficial community project**. It is not made or endorsed by Orcon, Itho, Vasco, ClimaRad, Nuaire or\nthe authors of ramses_esp. Use at your own risk."],[721,"This is by far the most common problem. The unit only executes commands from devices it is **bound** to."],[735,"Those are devices the app can't place yet, for examp